#speculation(title: [H1-Mediated TRPV1 Nociceptor Sensitisation as an Antihistamine-Analgesia Bridge])[
Histamine H1 signalling sensitises TRPV1 nociceptors: a TRPV1 antagonist abolished histamine-mediated TRPV1 sensitisation in dorsal-root-ganglion neurons and attenuated histaminergic itch in vivo @NikolaevaKoleva2021HistamineTRPV1, and mast-cell mediators acting on TRPV1+ sensory fibres drive allergic pain and itch, with repeated activation producing peripheral and central sensitisation @Kalangara2022TRPV1Histamine. Independent mouse work shows H1 antagonists exert anti-nociception across inflammatory and neuropathic pain models @Chen2023AntihistamineAnalgesia.

This suggests an indirect route by which H1 blockade — as with rupatadine — might reduce TRPV1-mediated muscle pain or soreness in ME/CFS: not by blocking TRPV1 directly, but by removing the histaminergic sensitising drive that lowers the nociceptor threshold. This dovetails with, and does not duplicate, the arteriolar TRPV1/ischemia cascade (@sec:trpv1-cascade). The histamine-to-TRPV1 step is shown directly in vitro and in animals; no human trial has demonstrated that an antihistamine reduces pain via TRPV1 de-sensitisation (translation gap), and the mouse analgesia may run through Kv7 channels rather than TRPV1 @Chen2023AntihistamineAnalgesia. (Certainty: 0.35)

_Falsifiable prediction:_ In a capsaicin or heat-pain quantitative sensory test, H1 blockade lowers TRPV1-mediated hyperalgesia in ME/CFS patients with concurrent mast-cell symptoms more than in patients without them, and this reduction correlates with a fall in a histamine-sensitive marker of nociceptor sensitisation.

*Consequence:* If validated, rupatadine's benefit on ME/CFS pain or soreness would gain a named mechanism — H1-to-TRPV1 de-sensitisation — separable from its PAF arm and from the vascular TRPV1 cascade, giving a cleaner read of which arm actually relieves pain.
] <spec:h1-trpv1-nociceptor-sensitisation>
